    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d295">

                <pb facs="0509" n="223" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg223"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 851.857Su8/36</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-04-05T13:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 5, 1916, 1 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 2 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4101. Your 3141, April 4, 4 [7] p. m., and 3144,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d295-f1"/>
                    April 4, 8 p. m.</p>
                <p>British Admiralty inform me after consulting their records that <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Sussex</hi> was never used as a transport or troopship,
                    and state further that route followed by <hi rendition="#italic">Sussex</hi> on
                    her last trip is not the one followed by transports or troopships proceeding
                    from England.</p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Ambassador</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
